{"qid":"Q1044","names":["Sierra Leone"],"title":"Sierra Leone","endonym":{"native":"Republic of Sierra Leone","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Sierra Leone achieved independence from Britain on 27 April 1961 under Prime Minister Milton Margai, having originated as a Crown Colony established in 1808 around the settler community founded in 1787 for freed slaves. The country experienced repeated military coups and single-party rule through the 1970s and 1980s under Siaka Stevens and Joseph Momoh. A devastating civil war (1991–2002), driven by the Revolutionary United Front under Foday Sankoh and fuelled by conflict diamonds, killed tens of thousands and displaced millions before UN and British forces restored order. Sierra Leone remains one of the world's lower-income economies but has maintained democratic elections since 2002.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Modern borders are treaty-defined and well established; the colonial-era frontier with French Guinea was fixed by the 1882 and 1895 Anglo-French conventions.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Sierra Leone","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sierra_Leone"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Sierra Leone Civil War","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sierra_Leone_Civil_War"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Milton Margai","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milton_Margai"}],"britannica":"place/Sierra-Leone","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Sierra Leone","rulers":[{"qid":"Q515657","name":"Siaka Stevens","start":1971,"end":1985,"image":"Siaka Stevens (I-002364, cropped, processing version).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Siaka%20Stevens%20